From 9d6c59d827aac1503bcc9c6b7aa28b309efd0f60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiron Builder <builder@chiron.local>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 10:24:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: give the ISP and its adapter the camera CMA pool

The board declares linux,camera_cma -- 272 MiB, reusable, 4 MiB aligned -- but
nothing referenced it, so both the ISP and its adapter fell back to the default
CMA area. That area is the one chiron-cma lends to the page cache, and a
fragmented 1.6 GiB of it cannot satisfy the order-10 contiguous allocations the
capture buffers need: REQBUFS on the hardware node failed with ENOMEM while
CmaFree still read a gigabyte, and dmesg showed cma_alloc failing against the
area named reserved rather than against camera_cma.

The factory Android device tree binds isp0 and
adapter0 to this same pool, by the same phandle. This restores that.

Change-Id: Ib0258bb6871f70ba75f3d6881c1916ae659a04a3
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/chiron.dts | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/chiron.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/chiron.dts
index f1d44c87e..7e1cc2701 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/chiron.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/chiron.dts
@@ -2243,8 +2243,10 @@
 
 &adapter0 {
 	status = "okay";
+	memory-region = <&camera_cma_reserved>;
 };
 
 &isp0 {
 	status = "okay";
+	memory-region = <&camera_cma_reserved>;
 };
